  "_comment": "Real capture from a Realtek RTL9210 USB-NVMe enclosure (E2M2 64GB), 2026-07-27 \u2014 the repo's first non-hand-authored NVMe fixture. smartctl auto-detects the bridge as type sntrealtek/protocol NVMe with no -d flag, so discovery and the NVMe path work through USB. Note this controller populates almost nothing: power-on hours, data units, power cycles and BOTH available_spare and its threshold read 0, which is 'feature not implemented', not 'spare exhausted' \u2014 see nvmeAttributeHealth. Also note nvme_optional_admin_commands.self_test is false: the controller cannot run a device self-test at all, and 'smartctl -t long' on it prints 'Self-tests not supported' while exiting 0.",
